  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Bug from ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3866"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Archive groups allow users to create, delete, and purge single resources and recreate them after. When querying fcr:versions on one of these resources, the server returns a http 500. The cause of this is a NPE from when Fedora is using the memento datetime as tombstones are not mementos. This should be what is happening when using the Accept-Datetime header as well to query the resource.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
