  "description": "<p>Bug from <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3866\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-3866</a></p>\n\n<p>Archive groups allow users to create, delete, and purge single resources and recreate them after. When querying fcr:versions on one of these resources, the server returns a http 500. The cause of this is a NPE from when Fedora is using the memento datetime as tombstones are not mementos. This should be what is happening when using the Accept-Datetime header as well to query the resource.</p>",
